From 1261945a7bcd734920ac0c9037b9a7489c16b8b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:28:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] cuda : persistent MoE kernels for the q5_K / q6_K
 expert layers on sm_60

Three layers of Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q4_K_XL have other expert types (34, 38: q6_K down; 39: q5_K gate / up, q6_K
down) and still ran the stock MoE path. The multi-token MoE kernel gets
- q5_K gate / up rows: lanes load their 64 weights directly (1408 B rows do not fit the staging buffer), next row in
  flight during the current row's math;
- q6_K down rows: 210 B superblocks leave the second superblock of a row 2 B aligned, so lanes load aligned words
  and funnel-shift; 6-bit quants minus 32 go straight to half2 pairs, 4 int8 scales per 64 weights.
The single-token case of these layers uses the multi-token kernel at T = 1.

2x P100, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q4_K_XL: no speculation tg128 120.2 -> 125.7 t/s; MTP prod sampler 8 x 256: 179.2 t/s
(acceptance varied, 171.8 before). Wikitext KLD vs the stock ub=1 base: ub=6 0.00422, ub=1 0.00434 (both slightly
lower than before).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
